&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 data-lfile-container=&quot;1ce32211-d6ec-4469-b6c1-aef738b09b30&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Discovery team at Anthropic is organized around the north star goal of building an AI scientist – a system capable of solving the long-term reasoning challenges and basic capabilities necessary to push the scientific and technological frontier.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re expanding our work on engineering and the applied sciences. Our goal is to contribute to training Claude to invent, design, and engineer across every discipline and scale, reliably and safely: new manufacturing and experimental techniques, processes, materials, devices, instruments, machines, energy systems, and factories. We want this work to accelerate science and technology and benefit people widely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To achieve these goals, we&#39;re seeking exceptional machine learning researchers with deep expertise in training and evaluating frontier models. In this role, you&#39;ll work end to end across the model stack, developing training environments, rewards, data, and evaluations that measure and improve Claude&#39;s performance on complex engineering and scientific tasks, and carrying what works into production training runs. You&#39;ll collaborate closely with researchers, engineers, and partners across Anthropic and industry to build AI systems that can engage in all phases of research and development, and that learn from real-world feedback. A background in engineering or the sciences is a plus but not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and study reinforcement learning environments, rewards, and training data that improve Claude&#39;s capabilities in engineering and the applied sciences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create benchmarks and evaluation frameworks that measure model performance on realistic engineering and scientific workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop simulation-based training environments and verifiers, working with domain experts to validate them against real-world data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop approaches to long-horizon task completion, multi-agent collaboration, and complex reasoning essential for real engineering and research work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research how models can learn efficiently from experiments and real-world feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Study how environments and rewards behave in large-scale training, including robustness, calibration, and generalization, so that training produces models that are both capable and well aligned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale research ideas from prototype to production training runs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with domain experts and industry partners to build and test what Claude invents, designs, and engineers, and turn that feedback into training and evaluation signal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help chart how Claude’s engineering capabilities reach real-world use: where they matter most, what stands in the way of adoption, and how that should shape research priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and hands-on experience with a modern machine learning framework such as PyTorch or JAX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience training or evaluating machine learning models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of machine learning research: forming hypotheses, designing and running experiments, and drawing sound conclusions from the results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to implement your own research ideas and diagnose problems in complex systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn unfamiliar technical fields quickly and work productively with experts in them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication and a collaborative approach to solving problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement about improving Claude’s scientific capabilities and the downstream impact on science and technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to developing AI that is safe and beneficial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with reinforcement learning and pre-training on large language models, including environment and reward design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with large-scale language model training, evaluation, and inference pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Published research or practical experience in AI for science or engineering, or in long-horizon reasoning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree or work experience in an engineering or applied science discipline, such as mechanical, electrical, materials, chemical, aerospace, systems, or manufacturing engineering, applied physics, or computational simulation&lt;/li&gt;
