&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nonprofits, universities and other mission-driven organizations do some of the hardest work in the world, usually with small teams and little technical capacity. As a Scaled Account Manager in Beneficial Deployments, you will be the person a named book of these organizations can rely on. You will own each customer relationship after the first conversation, including commercials, activation and the conversations that turn a new deployment into everyday use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits on the Scaled Sales team within Beneficial Deployments, the part of Anthropic that brings Claude to mission-driven organizations sooner and further than the market would on its own. You will work with little to no dedicated Customer Success support, so you are both the seller and the person who helps a customer get real value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That is only possible if you work differently. You will use Claude to take on the short-horizon tasks that consume a book like this, and spend your time on strategic conversations. The role will also change. As we automate more of this work, the book will take less of your time, and that time moves to growth: deeper work with your highest-potential accounts, launches, events and programs that reach many more organizations. We are hiring someone who wants that: someone who will automate parts of their own job and move on to the next hard problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own a named book of nonprofit and education customers.&lt;/strong&gt; Take over existing relationships and run them end to end: retention, seat growth, plan moves and new contacts inside each organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive activation yourself.&lt;/strong&gt; Help priority customers in the segment go from purchased seats to weekly use, starting with where staff lose the most time: fundraising, grant writing, reporting and program operations at nonprofits, or research support, teaching and administration in higher ed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate your own work.&lt;/strong&gt; Use Claude to handle account research, follow-ups, usage reviews and routine questions, then share what works so the whole team can use it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spend your time on strategic conversations.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with executive directors, operations leads, and IT and academic leaders at universities to find the use cases that matter to their mission and agree what success looks like.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spot who is ready for more.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify customers moving from individual productivity toward redesigned workflows, build the case, and bring in Applied AI or other specialists when they qualify for deeper support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build programs, not one-offs.&lt;/strong&gt; When ten customers have the same problem, create a playbook, webinar or cohort that solves it once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the voice of your book.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring what you hear to Product, Marketing, Support and Operations, and work across those teams to get customer problems fixed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Where your time goes as we automate&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role starts mostly account-facing. Over roughly the first six months, we expect Claude to take on much of the routine work, and your time shifts toward growth. Examples of where it goes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deeper with priority accounts.&lt;/strong&gt; Spend real time with the 10 to 15% of your book that can move from individual productivity to redesigned workflows, and get them there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quarterly launches.&lt;/strong&gt; Beneficial Deployments brings new offerings to the nonprofit and education community each quarter. Help drive them: coordinate across Marketing, Comms and partner teams, and make sure your customers benefit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Events.&lt;/strong&gt; Help shape and run the events, local and eventually international, that become a core part of how we reach new organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New signups and scaled partnerships.&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the motions that bring new organizations onto Claude, including partner channels and programs for segments we don&#39;t yet serve well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The exact mix will change, and you will help decide it. Part of the job is working out which tasks should be automated and which still deserve a person&#39;s time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You may be a good fit if you have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3+ years of account management or customer success experience with nonprofit or higher education customers, with a proven track record of growing retention and driving adoption of new technology&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have owned customer relationships in an account management or customer success role, and can point to accounts you grew, retained or turned around&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use AI in your own work today, and can show a workflow you built that gave you real time back&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bring structure to unfamiliar problems, and can move from a messy situation to a clear plan quickly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have run multi-step programs or projects with several stakeholders and kept them on track&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have got things done through people you did not manage, across teams in a larger organization&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stay effective when your job changes, and would see automating part of your role as a win&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Can explain AI plainly to people who are skeptical, busy or new to it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Care about the mission of nonprofits and educational institutions, and about AI being developed and deployed safely&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strong candidates may also&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have built something from zero, such as a company, a product, a sales motion or a new program, or been an early employee at a startup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have a consulting background, with experience across many sectors and problem types&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have worked at an AI-native company or sold AI products, or moved from business development into owning accounts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have worked in or with nonprofits, foundations, Universities or other mission-driven organizations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understand how nonprofits and universities buy, including boards, funders, procurement cycles and tight budgets&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have used usage data to prioritize a large book of accounts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$222,800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$290,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Partner Marketing Lead, APAC, reporting to the Global Head of Partner Marketing, to own partner marketing end to end across a region where partners are central to how Claude reaches enterprises. As our founding APAC Partner Marketing leader, you&#39;ll set the plan for the region rather than execute one set elsewhere: you&#39;ll build the operating model, carry partner pipeline goals, and turn our work with hyperscale cloud providers, global and regional systems integrators, resellers, and technology partners into a regional go-to-market motion that creates pipeline and drives adoption of Claude.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The central challenge is sequencing: ANZ, ASEAN, India, Japan, and Korea differ in their partner ecosystems, buyers, languages, and maturity. In some, local partners are the main route to enterprise customers, and India&#39;s systems integrators also deliver for customers worldwide. You&#39;ll decide where to invest first, where a global or partner-led program is enough for now, and where to wait.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role calls for the seniority to lead a regional organization and the willingness to start hands-on with a very small team, defining the regional team plan and then hiring and managing the team as headcount opens. The role covers the whole region, including Japan, where you&#39;ll build on an established Partner Marketing presence, so that partners and sales teams experience one connected regional approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the APAC partner marketing strategy, annual plan, and investment priorities, aligned with global Partner Marketing, the regional Partnerships business plan, and APAC sales leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decide which markets and partners to prioritize, in what order, and through which motions, and revisit those choices as the business changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Partner Marketing with regional and global leadership, and make clear recommendations on tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the regional operating model, including planning, intake, approvals, reporting, and how global programs are adapted for local markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the regional team plan and make the case for where to add capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, manage, and develop the team as headcount opens, and set the standard for partner marketing in the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a network of regional agencies and vendors to extend the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build joint marketing plans with priority partners, starting with hyperscale cloud providers and their co-sell and marketplace motions, alongside global and regional systems integrators, resellers, and technology partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip partners to market and sell Claude on their own, with localized campaigns, content, and workshops they can run with their own teams and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the regional partner calendar, including joint campaigns, executive engagements, workshops, partner events, and regional partner summits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set pipeline and adoption goals with Partnerships and sales leadership, and take ownership of the results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect partner activity to priority accounts and open opportunities so that partner and direct sales motions reinforce each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the regional pipeline of partner customer stories and public proof points&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the regional partner marketing budget and market development funds, with strong financial discipline and a focus on return&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize partner co-investment and negotiate effectively with vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how success is measured, including sourced and influenced pipeline and adoption of Claude, and use results to decide where to invest and what to stop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align the regional plan to the International Partnerships business plan, working with its leadership on overall goals and day to day with subregional and country partnerships leaders and partner managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with APAC sales leaders on account priorities and where partners can help open or advance deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with APAC Field Marketing so that field and partner programs run from one regional plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with global Partner Marketing on partners that span regions, such as cloud providers and global systems integrators, as well as Product Marketing, Customer Marketing, Communications, and Marketing Operations, and bring regional partner feedback back into their plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;14+ years of B2B enterprise technology marketing, with significant experience in partner or channel marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning partner or channel marketing strategy for a region or multiple markets, including priorities and investment decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading marketing programs across multiple Asia-Pacific markets, with strong awareness of how those markets differ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience hiring and managing marketers, or clear leadership experience to build a regional team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building programs with cloud providers, systems integrators, resellers, or distributors, and an understanding of co-sell and partner-led pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of contributing to significant pipeline or revenue goals, with strong analytics and attribution skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing substantial marketing budgets, including partner co-funding or market development funds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building programs and processes from the ground up, and willingness to do hands-on work while the team grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with sales leaders, partner executives, and senior stakeholders, and to move priorities forward with people you don&#39;t manage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to make thoughtful decisions with incomplete information, and comfort with ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication with executive and regional audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Care about the societal impacts of AI and about helping organizations adopt AI responsibly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling a partner or channel marketing function in APAC at an enterprise software or cloud company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading marketing with cloud providers, systems integrators, and resellers or distributors, including owning the pipeline that came from that work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a regional team across several APAC markets in partner or field marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as the first partner or field marketing leader in a new region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing AI/ML or other complex technical products to enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing with AWS, Microsoft, or Google Cloud in APAC, including co-sell and marketplace motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching or scaling a reseller or partner program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with partners, agencies, or industry organizations in the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in one or more Asia-Pacific languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of regional regulatory and compliance requirements for marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Claude or other AI tools to scale marketing work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
