&lt;li&gt;&l

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Associate Account Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At New Relic, we believe in a virtuous cycle where customer success fuels improved revenue performance. Our Associate Account Manager role is an integral support function within our pod structure that sits at the intersection of Customer Success, Sales, and Product. Focused on supporting the retention and health of our existing customer base, you will work alongside Account Managers and Account Executives to drive customer adoption, manage operational workflows, and assist with renewals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are passionate about building strong customer relationships, eager to grow in a quota-carrying environment, and looking to build a foundation in tech sales or customer success, this is the role for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Revenue &amp;amp; Retention Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pod Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as an operational and tactical contributor within a unified pod structure. Assist Account Executives and Account Managers with whitespace analysis, scheduling and organizing enablement sessions with Technical Success Managers, and preparing materials to help uncover new growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Renewal &amp;amp; Account Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the execution of contract renewals for direct and partner-managed agreements. Maintain regular check-ins with operational decision-makers, champions, and end-users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Churn Mitigation Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Help monitor account health, usage patterns, and BCM burn rates. Flag &quot;at-risk&quot; or low-engagement accounts early to senior team members and help execute strategic action plans to drive customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expansion Assistance:&lt;/strong&gt; Assist in identifying basic upsell and cross-sell opportunities, supporting Pay-As-You-Go (PAYG) customer outreach, and helping convert usage into expanded subscriptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cultivate Customer Success &amp;amp; Adoption&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Journey Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Account Executives on key customer milestones, helping handle day-to-day administrative and account support queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Review &amp;amp; Planning Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Help coordinate schedule logistics, slide decks, and data preparation for Customer Business Reviews (CBRs), Account Plans, and renewal discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adoption &amp;amp; Onboarding:&lt;/strong&gt; Assist during customer onboarding phases by organizing Account Health Checks, tracking Business Value Assessments, and scheduling customer enablement sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Advocacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Sales, Operations, Customer Solutions, Legal, and Collections to help resolve routine customer issues and navigate administrative processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Execution &amp;amp; Data Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Value Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop proficiency in articulating New Relic’s value proposition and product messaging in client-facing communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; Pipeline Hygiene:&lt;/strong&gt; Analyze customer usage data and assist in pipeline reporting. Maintain accurate record-keeping in Salesforce, ensuring buying programs, renewal dates, contact information, and sentiment are kept up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role Requires:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure or background in customer success, sales operations, account management, or business development (SaaS industry preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of quota support, contract administrative processes, or renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to build rapport with key technical and operational contacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with experience working with basic datasets (e.g., usage metrics, CRM data) to report on account activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, showing strong team collaboration and customer empathy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization and time-management skills, with a track record of multi-tasking effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Workspace, Salesforce (or similar CRM), MS Excel, and PowerPoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic familiarity with Observability, Application Performance Monitoring, or DevOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with consumption-based business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to structured sales methodologies (e.g., Challenger Sale, Command of the Message, MEDDPICC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eagerness to learn and develop into a full quota-carrying Account Manager role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in European languages is welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note visa support or sponsorship is not available for this position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.2;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-Hybrid #LI-JJ2&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fostering a diverse, welcoming and inclusive environment is important to us. We work hard to make everyone feel comfortable bringing their best, most authentic selves to work every day. We celebrate our talented Relics’ different backgrounds and abilities, and recognize the different paths they took to reach us – including nontraditional ones. Their experiences and perspectives inspire us to make our products and company the best they can be. We’re looking for people who feel connected to our mission and values, not just candidates who check off all the boxes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you require a reasonable accommodation to complete any part of the application or recruiting process, please reach out to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:resume@newrelic.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;resume@newrelic.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in empowering all Relics to achieve professional and business success through a flexible workforce model. This model allows us to work in a variety of workplaces that best support our success, including fully office-based, fully remote, or hybrid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In compliance with applicable law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work and to complete employment eligibility verification. Note: Our stewardship of the data of thousands of customers means that a criminal background check is required to join New Relic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We will consider qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records based on individual circumstances and in accordance with applicable law including, but not limited to, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sfgov.org/olse/sites/default/files/FCO%20poster2020.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headhunters and recruitment agencies may not submit resumes/CVs through this website or directly to managers. New Relic does not accept unsolicited headhunter and agency resumes, and will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with New Relic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New Relic develops and distributes encryption software and technology that complies with U.S. export controls and licensing requirements. Certain New Relic roles require candidates to pass an export compliance assessment as a condition of employment in any global location. If relevant, we will provide more information later in the application process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates are evaluated based on qualifications, regardless of race, religion, ethnicity, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression or identity, age, disability, neurodiversity, veteran or marital status, political viewpoint, or other legally protected characteristics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review our Applicant Privacy Notice at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://newrelic.com/termsandconditions/applicant-privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://newrelic.com/termsandconditions/applicant-privacy-policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Are you looking to take the next step in your sales career? Join New Relic, a leader in observability and application performance monitoring, where you can transition from an inbound-focused role to a key player on our outbound-driven Business Development team. You&#39;ll be a key part of our go-to-market strategy, joining a high-energy team that&#39;s at the forefront of building our pipeline. We&#39;re looking for individuals who are passionate about sales and keen to develop their expertise in an outbound-focused role.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll be supported by personalised coaching, world-class tools, and significant opportunities for career growth. At New Relic, hard work is celebrated, teamwork is a core value, and every success is shared. This is a chance to build a lasting sales career with a company that believes in investing in its people.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generate new business&lt;/strong&gt;: Create new opportunities through outbound cold calling, personalised email outreach, and social selling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualify leads&lt;/strong&gt;: Understand customer needs and align them with New Relic&#39;s solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate&lt;/strong&gt;: Partner with Account Executives to research target accounts and create tailored outreach strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage pipeline&lt;/strong&gt;: Maintain consistent communication to nurture early-stage opportunities and grow your prospect pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceed metrics&lt;/strong&gt;: Meet daily, weekly, and monthly targets for qualified meetings and pipeline contribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role Requires&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales experience&lt;/strong&gt;: Proven experience in a prospecting role, with a strong emphasis on your potential to succeed in an outbound environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A collaborative approach&lt;/strong&gt;: The ability to work closely with colleagues and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication skills&lt;/strong&gt;: Excellent written and verbal communication to engage with prospects at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&l

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you a recent graduate with a passion for sales and technology, eager to kickstart your career in a dynamic SaaS environment? At New Relic, we&#39;re seeking an Associate Sales Development Representative to join our team and be at the forefront of our go-to-market strategy. This role is perfect for ambitious individuals looking to develop their sales skills while working in an environment that values innovation, personal growth, and professional excellence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join New Relic?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At New Relic, we offer a transformative experience to kickstart your career in sales and in the cutting-edge world of observability. Our Sales team is at the forefront of our go-to-market strategy, partnering closely with Account Executives (AEs) to deliver impactful business outcomes for our customers. You’ll join a collaborative, high-energy team with personalized coaching, world-class tools, and significant opportunities for career growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At New Relic, we believe in supporting our team with the resources, mentorship, and opportunities to build a lasting career in sales. You’ll be part of a culture where hard work is rewarded, teamwork drives success, and every win is celebrated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us in building something great. Apply now!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an SDR, you will be the first point of contact for prospects and customers reaching out to New Relic about their digital transformation journey. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage inbound leads from email, phone, and Live Sales Chat within your assigned region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualify prospective customers interested in New Relic solutions as part of their digital transformation journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze customer needs in terms of current business obstacles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align with account managers to progress business-ready opportunities and ensure a smooth handover for the customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create qualified business leads to achieve a quarterly quota, consistently meeting or exceeding targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master social selling and communication skills, actively using various tools including social media and web-based tools to engage with customers and prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve a high level of collaboration within the Sales Development team and with key stakeholders in Sales and Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role requires&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Degree&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest in technology with a customer-first mindset and enthusiasm for understanding technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grit, drive, and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, goal-oriented environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for sales, with aspirations to grow into a closing role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive and agile mindset, enthusiastic and genuinely passionate about this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills (written and verbal) with the ability to engage prospects at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilience and a positive attitude when facing challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time management skills with a sharp focus on goals and a clear approach for achieving them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with cold calling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid position. Three days per week in our Dublin office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a customer-facing role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient attitude and determination to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to objections and turn “no” into “let’s talk further.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach to working with teams and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native proficiency in second European language (German, French, Dutch, Spanish, Italian, Polish)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cold calling experience: previous experience in a role that required outbound cold calling and willingness and comfort in making outbound calls daily as a primary function of the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this position.&lt;/p&gt;
